Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 06:40:22 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] gateway: a Copilot account is asked tool search as
 advanced-tool-use, the name its Messages API takes (#3475)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Claude Desktop's gateway mode runs Claude Code with experimental betas
off, so its "Enable tool search" asks tool search as Bedrock's and
Vertex's tool-search-tool-2025-10-19. Copilot's /v1/messages and
count_tokens turn that name away — 400 "unsupported beta header(s):
tool-search-tool-2025-10-19" — so every Desktop session's first request
failed and Claude Code turned tool search off for it, sending every tool
schema inline. Copilot serves the same deferred tools as Anthropic's own
advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20.

Root cause: betas() fitted betas one way only — Bedrock's names — and
forwarded everything else as the agent asked it. A Copilot account
(p.Account.Agent == "copilot") is now renamed through copilotBetas before
the dedupe, so both names asked together go once, and every other
provider is asked the name the agent asked. /v1/messages, count_tokens
and a body's anthropic_beta all go through betas().

RED -> GREEN: TestCopilotToolSearchBeta drives the gateway handler to a
fake Copilot API that refuses the Bedrock name as the reporter's log
does. At 01468003 (test kept, betas.go as before):
  FAIL copilot_tool_search_test.go:77: Messages, betas
  "tool-search-tool-2025-10-19": 400 {"error":{"message":"Copilot:
  unsupported beta header(s): tool-search-tool-2025-10-19", ...}}
With the change: both tests pass, and TestUserBetas* and
TestSignInBetaStaysWithMagpie still pass.

Run at this head (GOTOOLCHAIN=go1.26.8, temp HOME, pinned Go caches):
  go test -tags nogui ./internal/gateway/... -count=1   (one red, below)
  go vet ./...                                         exit 0
  GOOS=linux GOARCH=amd64 go vet -tags nogui ./...     exit 0
  GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go vet ./...               exit 0
  go build ./...                                       exit 0
  GOOS=linux GOARCH=amd64 go build -tags nogui ./...   exit 0
  GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go build ./...             exit 0
  gofmt -l on the changed files                        empty

Pre-existing red at 01468003, not from this change and not hidden:
TestClaudeClientCacheAbsentUnchanged (claude_client_cache_test.go:291,
"ordinary prompt changed"). It fails the same way with this branch's
betas.go stashed, so it is red on the clean base too.

Not tried: a real Copilot Business account and a real Claude Desktop
(no credentials here); GHE Copilot (same Agent == "copilot" branch).
